  "notes": "{寄|よ}せる is an ichidan verb meaning to bring close, gather, or direct toward something.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Pair: {寄|よ}る (intransitive: to approach, to stop by)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {椅子|いす}を{寄|よ}せる: to draw up a chair\n- {思|おも}いを{寄|よ}せる: to have feelings for someone\n- {信頼|しんらい}を{寄|よ}せる: to place trust in\n- {期待|きたい}を{寄|よ}せる: to place expectations on\n- {関心|かんしん}を{寄|よ}せる: to take interest in\n- {身|み}を{寄|よ}せる: to take shelter with\n\nCOMPOUND VERBS:\n- {寄|よ}せ{集|あつ}める: to gather together",
